<VI _name="lvai_typedef_discon.vi" description="Disconnect ONE control from its typedef - addressed by the same index path lvai_typedef_tree.vi lists - and save the file in place.\0A\0AIT OPENS THE VI IN THE IDE'S APPLICATION INSTANCE\2C AND THAT IS THE WHOLE POINT. {LV.Control} Discon Typedef from a helper that reached its target with a bare Open VI Reference TERMINATES LabVIEW\3A measured 2026-09-18\2C five runs across three probe shapes and two target files\2C with no entry in NI's own crash log and the target never written. A bare Open VI Reference resolves in the application instance the HELPER runs in - the AI addon's - while the IDE gesture a person performs by hand runs in the IDE's. Reached through Project\3AActive Project the same call answers code 0 and LabVIEW lives. So the hop is not a formality here\2C it is the difference between working and losing the session.\0A\0APRECONDITION\3A a project must be OPEN AND ACTIVE. Without one the first property node answers Error 1055 and nothing else runs\2C which is a clean refusal rather than a crash - and that refusal is deliberate\2C because the alternative is the bare open that kills LabVIEW.\0A\0AIT IS NOT RECURSIVE. Measured on a typedef nested inside a typedef\3A disconnecting the outer control left the inner one linked\2C so a chain needs one call per level. The caller walks the tree and addresses each.\0A\0AIT DESCENDS INTO BOTH CLUSTERS AND ARRAYS\2C the same way lvai_typedef_tree.vi does. Controls[] is declared on {LV.Cluster} and not on {LV.Array}\2C whose single child is reached through Array Element and comes back as ONE reference\3A both are read unconditionally and Select picks between them on Class Name\2C which keeps the descent one flat loop. The cast that does not apply fails harmlessly\2C its error deliberately unwired. An array contributes one segment like any other container and its only child index is 0.\0A\0ANothing is read back from the control afterwards. That is not known to matter for this method - a probe reading nothing back died the same way when the instance was wrong - but there is no reason to carry the risk.">
